  "body": "removal of the aria-haspopup attribute in the popover example.  It is understandably confusing calling this out and identifying it's purpose, without getting into the weeds of what it is, and how it's not 100% related to the popover attribute.  Instead of getting deep into that here, allude to ARIA having requirements related to the construction of a menu widget.\n\nthis PR also contains other minor typo fixes I noticed that I missed in my original PR.\n\ncloses #9153\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9262/popover.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 9, 2023, 3:11 PM UTC (6e018f0)\">/popover.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9262/cf9625f...6e018f0/popover.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 9, 2023, 3:11 PM UTC (6e018f0)\">diff</a> )",
